<DocsLayout title="Install Haft" description="Install the Haft CLI and initialize its governance surfaces for your coding agent.">
  <h1>Install &amp; init</h1>

  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/releases/tag/v9.0.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v9.0.0</a>
    is the current release.
  </p>

  <h2>Install the binary</h2>

  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/m0n0x41d/haft/main/install.sh | bash</code></pre>

  <p>
    The installer places <code>haft</code> in a writable binary directory,
    normally <code>~/.local/bin</code>. v9 requires no Elixir, OTP, or BEAM
    toolchain and ships no Open-Sleigh runtime. The optional
    <code>haft-embed</code> compatibility sidecar is independent of the core
    governance product.
  </p>

  <h2>Initialize one project</h2>

  <pre><code>cd /path/to/project
haft init                    # interactive host selection in a terminal
haft init --claude           # Claude MCP, skills, and CLAUDE.md section
haft init --codex            # Codex MCP, skills, and AGENTS.md section
haft init --core-only        # project core only
haft init --all              # full Claude + Codex integrations</code></pre>

  <p>
    Bare non-interactive <code>haft init</code> fails before writing instead of
    guessing a host. Scripts and CI must pass an explicit flag. Use
    <code>--local</code> when you want supported skill carriers inside the
    repository, and <code>--mcp-only</code> only with an explicit host target.
  </p>

  <div class="callout-warn">
    <p>
      <strong>Restart the host after init or upgrade.</strong> A running MCP
      process keeps using the binary and skill catalog it already loaded.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Upgrade from v8.1</h2>

  <p>
    Stop Haft writers and back up both the project <code>.haft/</code> directory
    and <code>~/.haft/projects/&lt;project-id&gt;/haft.db</code> before the first v9
    start. The database migration is forward-only across this boundary.
  </p>

  <p>
    After a successful install, v9 removes only
    <code>~/.haft/runtimes/open-sleigh/current</code>. It preserves
    <code>~/.open-sleigh/</code> user data and
    <code>~/.haft/runtimes/haft-embed/</code>. Migrate scripts that call
    <code>haft run</code> or <code>haft harness</code> to host-agent work or an
    external runner using the WorkCommission lifecycle.
  </p>

  <p>
    Follow the complete <a href="/docs/migration">v8.1 to v9.0 migration and rollback guide</a>
    before opening a working project ledger with v9.
  </p>

  <h2>Verify the connection</h2>

  <pre><code>haft version
haft doctor</code></pre>

  <p>
    Then restart the coding agent in the project and request
    <code>/h-status</code>. A source-level check confirms only the checkout; an
    installed-runtime readiness claim needs evidence from the exact installed
    candidate.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
